			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1580,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Read TierSchemeAssets from .env.Land as env fallback\n\nAdd the helper function `ReadTierValueFromEnvFile` to build.rs that walks up the directory tree from `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR` (up to 5 ancestors) looking for `.env.Land` or `.env.Land.Sample` to resolve the `TierSchemeAssets` key. The resolution priority is: process environment variable first, then the env file, then the hard-coded default of `\"Embedded\"`.\n\nThis mirrors the file-reading logic already used by `PropagateTierGating` in the Rust tier system, ensuring the tauri.conf.json mutation in build.rs agrees with the cfg-gated Rust code even when a shell has a stale exported `$TierSchemeAssets` from a previous build tier. If the env file is found but the key is absent, the function returns `None` immediately rather than falling through to a parent directory — preventing accidental cross-project key leakage.",
			"SHA": "4ba376b9241d0f9cc58e68f6cb1be03affa8000c"
		}
	],
